---
// Serra 2.0 Landing Page

import '../styles/global.css';
import Navigation from '../components/navbar.astro';

// Base URL for GitHub Pages
const baseUrl = '/serra2';

// Page metadata
const pageTitle = "Serra 2.0 - Reimagining Serra Angel";
const pageDescription = "An art project celebrating Serra Angel through contemporary artistic interpretations";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <meta name="description" content={pageDescription}>
  <title>{pageTitle}</title>
</head>
<body>
  <Navigation currentPage="home" />

  <section class="hero" id="home">
    <div class="hero-content">
      <h1>Serra 2.0</h1>
      <p>A contemporary reimagining of the iconic Serra Angel through the eyes of diverse artists</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about" id="about">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title">About the Project</h2>
      <div class="about-content">
        <blockquote class="serra-quote">
          « Born with wings of light and a sword of faith,
          this heavenly incarnation embodies with fury and purity. »
        </blockquote>
        
        <div class="about-text">
          <p>
            <b>Serra Angel.</b> Every player knows this iconic card. It has existed since the very beginning of the game—the only creature to have survived thirty years of evolution! Where are its former foes now, Sengir Vampire or Shivan Dragon?
          </p>
          <p>
            The angel, however, has aged, losing some of its power. Designers have imagined successors, such as Avacyn, Angel of Hope in 2016, but none can truly compete with the romance and nostalgia associated with Serra Angel.
          </p>
          <p>
            Artists now wish to pay tribute to her through original creations. Each presents a new version of the Angel, their own 2.0 vision.
          </p>
          <p>
            The first exhibitions will take place in France in 2026; dates are currently under discussion. The framing of each piece was defined in collaboration with each artist. Every work is accompanied by a presentation of the artist as well as a way to contact them.
          </p>
          <p>
            This exhibition is organized by DrChoc and Kevin Altered. The works are part of our personal collections, the Serra 2.0 exhibition collection, or are on loan from the artists; we kindly ask that they be treated with respect.
          </p>
          <p>
            We hope you enjoy this exhibition, which offers a fresh perspective on Serra Angel.
          </p>
          <p>
            Each piece in this collection offers a unique perspective, from traditional painting to digital illustration and three-dimensional sculpture, united by their reverence for the source material and their bold artistic vision.
          </p>
          <div class="article-image2">
            <img src=`${baseUrl}/SerraRevised.jpg` alt="Serra Angel from Revised edition">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Serra 2.0 Project. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>